      en: "The Pieterskerk in Leiden is a Gothic church from the 14th century. It was built between 1390 and 1400 and is dedicated to Saint Peter. The church is known as the burial place of John Robinson, leader of the Pilgrim Fathers. The church played an important role in Dutch history, especially during the Siege of Leiden in 1574. Inside are numerous tomb slabs and murals. The organ dates from 1883. Pieterskerk is now used mainly for cultural events, having been deconsecrated in 1971. About 120,000 people visit annually.",
