      en: "The Van Nelle Factory in Rotterdam is a UNESCO World Heritage site and a masterpiece of early 20th-century industrial architecture. It was built between 1925 and 1931 to a design by Leendert van der Vlugt in the New Building style. The factory was known for processing coffee, tea, and tobacco. The building features a transparent facade of steel and glass. It is considered a symbol of modern industrial culture. Today the factory houses offices and creative businesses. The complex covers 12 hectares. Guided tours and events take place annually.",
